# Machine: MareNostrum 5 (BSC)

I am running on a MareNostrum 5 login node (alogin = ACC accelerated partition).

- Cluster: MN5 ACC (4x H100 64GB per node), BSC
- Scheduler: SLURM — QoS: acc_ehpc (production), acc_debug, acc_interactive
- Account/project: <FILL IN: e.g. ehpc1003 — verify with `bsc_acct`>
- Workspace: /gpfs/scratch/<project>/<user>  (e.g. /gpfs/scratch/ehpc1003/vlk142020)
- Code convention: ~/projects/<repo> (symlink into /gpfs/projects/<project>/<user>/)
- Filesystem is GPFS — see the hpc-mn5 plugin's gpfs-hang-resilience reference
  before debugging hung reads
- NO direct outbound internet — goes via the team proxy tunnel (git-proxy /
  gost; see valka-ai/bsc-onboarding docs/setup-proxy.md)
- CUDA env: `source ~/cu128.sh` (or cu122.sh)
- Quota/accounting: `bsc_quota`, `bsc_acct`
- Slack job notifier: `source ~/scripts/job_notifier` in sbatch scripts
